    <briefdescription>
<para>Windows implementations of Daemon platform helpers. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Windows: <computeroutput>hideDockIcon()</computeroutput> is a no-op — no dock icon exists when no window is created. <computeroutput>spawnDaemon(uuid)</computeroutput> uses <computeroutput>CreateProcessW</computeroutput> with <computeroutput>DETACHED_PROCESS | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>installPlatformProcessCleanup()</computeroutput> creates a Job Object with <computeroutput>JOB_OBJECT_LIMIT_KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>releasePlatformProcessCleanup()</computeroutput> closes the Job Object handle.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>NEXUS PROCESS MESSAGE THREAD — all functions are called from Daemon::start() / Daemon::stop() or <ref refid="class_e_n_d_application_1a96fc235a4618e12e65fb65d24578a554" kindref="member">ENDApplication::initialise()</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
